# Dev Notes 53 — Runtime Execute-Action Public Envelope Dispatch v1

**Date:** 2026-06-20  
**Prepared branch:** `runtime-execute-action-public-envelope-dispatch-v1`  
**Actual integration path:** Uploaded directly to GitHub `main` instead of a feature branch / PR merge.  
**Repo:** `Main-Michael-Sparks/runtime-dev-repo`  
**Source truth:** GitHub `main` after direct upload.  
**Status:** Uploaded directly to `main` and main-inspected for the declared public raw action-envelope dispatch scope. Assistant sandbox syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted public-envelope dispatch smoke, existing execute-action/nativeWorkerBackend behavior smokes, current contract-chain smokes, broader mock/static lifecycle/worker regression smokes, artifact/package guard, package extraction/recheck, and Michael local Windows/MINGW64 real-runtime checks for both public raw-envelope dispatch and the existing nativeWorkerBackend executeAction path passed. The normal feature-branch / PR branch-verification gate was skipped because the candidate was uploaded directly to `main`; direct `main` inspection was used instead.

---

## 1. Purpose

This work extends the existing execute-action chain upward so public `executeAction(...)` can accept raw Runtime Dev action envelopes for the current built-in route:

```text
text.generate -> nativeWorkerBackend -> native-worker.default
```

The completed descriptor chain is:

```text
raw actionEnvelope
  -> Capability Bus action validation
  -> Capability Router route plan
  -> Capability Service plan
  -> Backend Adapter plan
  -> Capability Execution plan
  -> accepted execute-action plan
  -> execute-action orchestration descriptor
  -> existing runExecuteAction(...)
  -> nativeWorkerBackend execution seam
  -> existing parent runtime substrate
```

This is not a second execution path. It is a small public/input dispatch composition seam above the already accepted execute-action behavior seam.

